* rework api to follow this base layout /api/v<>/orgs/{org}/collections/{collection}
* collect, save and display ansible_facts
* create a secret backend (local and vault/openbao backed), both for ingestion, export or first time generation (init a DB password for example)

Webhooks:
* accept webhooks per collection
* accept payloads format from common CI services (github, gitea/forgeo, gitlab, jenkins) and add a generic default format

Tests:
* if tests are dependent on the DB, create per tests DBs with a test dataset (past jobs, status, etc)
* add a small utility to load this test dataset for developpement

Playbook page:
* rename playbook into playbook collections http://localhost:8080/playbooks
* in the table, add a last run collumn (date)
* for the status, display K/N Ok (ratio of hosts ok) instead of binary OK/Failure
* add a collum/button to go to a playbook run streaming page
* add a collum id with for example "hypervisors", and a one for the playbook with for example "hypervisor.yml"
* make the playbook and inventory file name clickable, and create a page displaying them (line number & color syntaxing appreciated)

Hosts Page http://localhost:8080/hosts
* remove the disappeared toggle, replace it with a dedicated "not seen in while (ghost icon)" page
* use the collection -> playbook -> host hierarchy tree in the list (collapsable tree, at least a the collection level, and if many host, also at the playbook level)
* don't change the title/upper bar of when selecting an host
* keep the last 3 run, but add a dedicated page to search older runs, specially ones with failures or changes (and optional threshold)
* add quick filter buttons to hide/unhide OK or skip tasks in the Task change container, hide skipped tasks by default

On the dashboard view:
* make runs clickable, if necessary give runs UUIDv7 in the backend

Backend
* allow for a per playbook frequency setting in strangle.yml file (wit default, min and max values in main configuration).
* replace /api/sync with a /api/v<>/orgs/{org}/collections/{collection}/sync

Authz:
* add notion of group (internal, ldap group, OAuth metadata (not sure which one)?, mapping to ownership of collections.
* support descreate user ownership of collection.
* only show collection you own/are member of in the ui

Sandboxing:
* deny FS writes to ansible
* make sure credentials used in one collection are not leveraged in another (specially don't leverage, $HOME/.ssh/)
